-- A FIRST PERSON VIEW, CAST IN POLITELANG
--
-- For every column of the picture, a ray is walked forward from where you are standing until it
-- meets a wall. How far it went decides how tall that slice of wall is drawn. That is the whole
-- of it, and it is enough to stand inside a room and look around.

please define the world:
    remember rows is an empty list
    add "################" to rows
    add "#..............#" to rows
    add "#..............#" to rows
    add "#....####...##.#" to rows
    add "#....#..#......#" to rows
    add "#....#..#...##.#" to rows
    add "#....####...##.#" to rows
    add "#..............#" to rows
    add "#....######....#" to rows
    add "#..............#" to rows
    add "#..##....##....#" to rows
    add "#..##....##....#" to rows
    add "#..............#" to rows
    add "#......##......#" to rows
    add "#..............#" to rows
    add "################" to rows
    give back rows
thank you for defining


-- Is the square at this place a wall?
please define a wall at with an ex and a why and a rows:
    check if ex is under 0:
        give back yes
    thanks
    check if why is under 0:
        give back yes
    thanks
    remember row is item the whole part of why plus 1 of rows or "################"
    remember cell is the letter the whole part of ex plus 1 of row or "#"
    give back cell is "#"
thank you for defining


-- Walls further away are drawn darker, so distance can be seen as well as measured.
please define dimmed with a shade and a far:
    remember amount is 1 minus far divided by 18
    remember kept is amount kept between 0.15 and 1
    give back the rounded version of shade times kept
thank you for defining


please remember rows is the world
please remember ex is 2.5
please remember why is 1.5
please remember facing is 0.6
please remember playing is yes

please open a canvas 100 across and 64 down

please keep going forever:
    check if not playing:
        stop repeating
    thanks

    -- Sky above the middle, floor below it.
    clear the canvas to the colour called "night" or 0
    fill a box from the point 0 and 0 to the point 99 and 31 in the colour with red 26 green 34 blue 48
    fill a box from the point 0 and 32 to the point 99 and 63 in the colour with red 40 green 34 blue 28

    -- One ray for every column across.
    repeat for every column from 0 to 99:
        remember angle is facing minus 0.45 plus column times 0.009
        remember dx is the cosine of angle
        remember dy is the sine of angle

        remember far is 0.0
        remember found is no
        keep going forever:
            change far to far plus 0.06
            check if far is over 18:
                stop repeating
            thanks
            check if a wall at with ex plus dx times far and why plus dy times far and rows:
                change found to yes
                stop repeating
            thanks
        thanks

        check if found:
            -- Straightening the distance stops the walls bending outward at the edges.
            remember straight is far times the cosine of angle minus facing
            remember tall is the rounded version of 30 divided by straight or 30
            remember half is tall kept between 1 and 31

            remember shade is dimmed with 200 and far
            remember wall is the colour with red shade green (dimmed with 190 and far) blue (dimmed with 165 and far)
            draw a line from the point column and 32 minus half to the point column and 32 plus half in wall
        thanks
    thanks

    reveal the canvas

    show ""
    show "  you are at {the rounded version of ex times 10} , {the rounded version of why times 10} tenths, looking {the rounded version of facing in degrees} degrees round"
    show "  forward, back, left, right, or done"
    ask "  > " as said

    remember step is 0.45
    check if said is "forward":
        remember nx is ex plus the cosine of facing times step
        remember ny is why plus the sine of facing times step
        check if not (a wall at with nx and ny and rows):
            change ex to nx
            change why to ny
        otherwise:
            show "  The wall does not move."
        thank you for checking
    otherwise if said is "back":
        remember bx is ex minus the cosine of facing times step
        remember by is why minus the sine of facing times step
        check if not (a wall at with bx and by and rows):
            change ex to bx
            change why to by
        thanks
    otherwise if said is "left":
        change facing to facing minus 0.3
    otherwise if said is "right":
        change facing to facing plus 0.3
    otherwise if said is "done":
        change playing to no
    otherwise:
        show "  I know forward, back, left, right and done."
    thank you for checking
thank you for repeating

please show ""
please show "  You step back out of it."
